# Book Management REST API - Educational Example

## Overview

This is a complete, well-documented REST API built with Node.js and Express.js that manages books using in-memory storage. The implementation follows REST conventions, includes comprehensive error handling with custom error classes, provides detailed JSDoc documentation for every function, and demonstrates best practices for educational purposes. The code is organized into logical sections with clear explanations of design decisions, patterns chosen, and why certain approaches were selected over alternatives.

## Project Structure

```
book-api/
├── package.json          # Dependencies and scripts
├── app.js                # Main application file
└── README.md             # Usage instructions
```

## File 1: package.json

```json
{
  "name": "book-management-api",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Educational REST API for managing books with detailed documentation",
  "main": "app.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node app.js",
    "dev": "nodemon app.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "nodemon": "^3.0.1"
  }
}
```

**Explanation**: We use Express as our web framework because it's the most popular Node.js framework for building APIs, with excellent middleware support and a large ecosystem. Nodemon is included as a dev dependency for automatic server restarts during development. The package.json follows standard conventions with clear script names for starting the application.

## File 2: app.js - Complete Implementation

```javascript
/**
 * Book Management REST API
 * 
 * A comprehensive educational example demonstrating REST API design patterns,
 * error handling, validation, and documentation best practices using Node.js
 * and Express.js.
 * 
 * @module book-api
 * @author Educational Example
 * @version 1.0.0
 */

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 1: DEPENDENCIES AND CONFIGURATION
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Import Express framework for building the web server and API routes.
 * We choose Express because it provides a robust middleware system, 
 * simple routing API, and excellent community support.
 */
const express = require('express');

/**
 * Initialize Express application instance.
 * This creates our HTTP server with all built-in functionality.
 */
const app = express();

// Configuration constants for the application
const CONFIG = {
  PORT: process.env.PORT || 3000,           // Server port (default 3000)
  API_VERSION: 'v1',                       // API versioning strategy
  MAX_BOOKS: 1000,                         // Maximum books in storage
  VALID_RATING_RANGE: { min: 0, max: 5 },   // Valid rating range
  VALID_YEAR_RANGE: { min: 1450, max: 2024 } // Valid publication year range
};

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 2: DATA STORAGE AND MODELS
// ============================================================================

/**
 * In-memory data storage for books.
 * 
 * WHY IN-MEMORY STORAGE?
 * - Educational simplicity: No database setup required
 * - Fast access: O(1) lookups by ID, O(n) searches
 * - Easy to understand: Clear data structure visualization
 * - Stateless: Perfect for demonstrating REST principles
 * 
 * In production, you would replace this with a proper database (MongoDB, PostgreSQL, etc.)
 */
const books = [];

/**
 * Book model schema definition.
 * This serves as documentation for the expected book structure.
 */
const BOOK_SCHEMA = {
  id: { type: 'number', required: true, description: 'Unique identifier' },
  title: { type: 'string', required: true, minLength: 1, maxLength: 500 },
  author: { type: 'string', required: true, minLength: 1, maxLength: 200 },
  genre: { 
    type: 'string', 
    required: true,
    enum: ['Fiction', 'Non-Fiction', 'Science', 'Technology', 'History', 'Biography', 'Fantasy', 'Mystery'],
    description: 'Book category'
  },
  publishedYear: { 
    type: 'number', 
    required: true,
    min: CONFIG.VALID_YEAR_RANGE.min,
    max: CONFIG.VALID_YEAR_RANGE.max
  },
  rating: { 
    type: 'number', 
    required: false,
    default: 0,
    min: CONFIG.VALID_RATING_RANGE.min,
    max: CONFIG.VALID_RATING_RANGE.max
  }
};

/**
 * Auto-incrementing ID generator for new books.
 * Using a simple counter ensures unique IDs without database dependencies.
 */
let nextId = 1;

/**
 * Generate a unique ID for a new book.
 * @returns {number} Unique identifier
 */
function generateId() {
  return nextId++;
}

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 3: CUSTOM ERROR CLASSES
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Base error class for all custom errors in the application.
 * Extends JavaScript's built-in Error class with additional properties.
 */
class ApiError extends Error {
  /**
   * @param {string} message - Human-readable error message
   * @param {number} statusCode - HTTP status code (4xx client, 5xx server)
   * @param {string[]} [details] - Additional error details
   */
  constructor(message, statusCode, details = []) {
    super(message);
    this.statusCode = statusCode;
    this.details = details;
    this.isOperational = true; // Distinguishes operational errors from programming bugs

    // Maintain proper stack trace
    Error.captureStackTrace(this, this.constructor);
  }
}

/**
 * Client error: Resource not found (404).
 * Used when requested book doesn't exist.
 */
class NotFoundError extends ApiError {
  constructor(resource = 'resource', id = null) {
    const message = id 
      ? `${resource} with ID ${id} not found`
      : `${resource} not found`;
    super(message, 404);
  }
}

/**
 * Client error: Invalid request data (400).
 * Used for validation failures and malformed requests.
 */
class ValidationError extends ApiError {
  constructor(field, message) {
    const detail = field ? `${field}: ${message}` : message;
    super(`Validation failed: ${detail}`, 400, [{ field, message }]);
  }
}

/**
 * Server error: Internal server error (500).
 * Used for unexpected errors that shouldn't reach clients.
 */
class InternalServerError extends ApiError {
  constructor(message = 'Internal server error') {
    super(message, 500);
  }
}

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 4: MIDDLEWARE FUNCTIONS
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Request logging middleware.
 * Logs each request with timestamp, method, URL, and response time.
 * 
 * WHY LOGGING?
 * - Debugging: Track API usage patterns
 * - Performance monitoring: Identify slow endpoints
 * - Audit trail: Record all API interactions
 */
function requestLogger(req, res, next) {
  const startTime = Date.now();

  // Log request details
  console.log(`[${new Date().toISOString()}] ${req.method} ${req.originalUrl}`);

  // Capture response completion for timing
  res.on('finish', () => {
    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
    console.log(`  → ${res.statusCode} (${duration}ms)`);
  });

  next();
}

/**
 * JSON body parsing middleware with size limit.
 * Prevents oversized payloads and ensures proper content-type handling.
 */
app.use(express.json({ 
  limit: '10kb', // Limit request body to 10KB for security
  strict: true   // Only parse arrays and objects (not strings/numbers)
}));

/**
 * CORS middleware for cross-origin requests.
 * Enables testing from browsers and other services.
 */
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', '*');
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Headers', 'Origin, X-Requested-With, Content-Type, Accept');
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Methods', 'GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS');

  // Handle preflight requests
  if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
    return res.sendStatus(200);
  }
  next();
});

/**
 * Request validation middleware factory.
 * Creates reusable validation functions for different endpoints.
 */
function validateRequest(schema) {
  /**
   * Validate request body against schema.
   * @param {Object} req - Express request object
   * @param {Object} res - Express response object  
   * @param {Function} next - Express next middleware function
   */
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const errors = [];

    // Validate required fields
    for (const [field, rules] of Object.entries(schema)) {
      if (rules.required && !req.body[field]) {
        errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `is required`));
      }

      // Type validation
      if (req.body[field] !== undefined && req.body[field] !== null) {
        if (rules.type === 'string' && typeof req.body[field] !== 'string') {
          errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be a string`));
        } else if (rules.type === 'number' && typeof req.body[field] !== 'number') {
          errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be a number`));
        }

        // Range validation
        if (typeof req.body[field] === 'number') {
          if (rules.min !== undefined && req.body[field] < rules.min) {
            errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be at least ${rules.min}`));
          }
          if (rules.max !== undefined && req.body[field] > rules.max) {
            errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be at most ${rules.max}`));
          }
        }

        // Length validation for strings
        if (typeof req.body[field] === 'string') {
          if (rules.minLength && req.body[field].length < rules.minLength) {
            errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be at least ${rules.minLength} characters`));
          }
          if (rules.maxLength && req.body[field].length > rules.maxLength) {
            errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be at most ${rules.maxLength} characters`));
          }
        }

        // Enum validation
        if (rules.enum && !rules.enum.includes(req.body[field])) {
          errors.push(new ValidationError(field, `must be one of: ${rules.enum.join(', ')}`));
        }
      }
    }

    if (errors.length > 0) {
      return next(new ValidationError('request', `${errors.length} validation error(s)`));
    }

    next();
  };
}

/**
 * Global error handling middleware.
 * Catches all errors and formats consistent error responses.
 * 
 * WHY THIS PATTERN?
 * - Centralized error handling: One place for all error formatting
 * - Consistent API responses: Clients always get the same structure
 * - Security: Prevents leaking internal error details to clients
 */
function errorHandler(err, req, res, next) {
  // Log error details for debugging (not sent to client)
  console.error('Error:', {
    message: err.message,
    statusCode: err.statusCode,
    isOperational: err.isOperational,
    stack: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? err.stack : undefined
  });

  // Format error response based on error type
  const errorResponse = {
    success: false,
    error: {
      message: err.message,
      statusCode: err.statusCode || 500,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
    }
  };

  // Add details for validation errors
  if (err.details && err.details.length > 0) {
    errorResponse.error.details = err.details;
  }

  // Send formatted response
  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json(errorResponse);
}

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 5: ROUTE HANDLERS
// ============================================================================

/**
 * GET /books - List all books with optional filtering.
 * 
 * QUERY PARAMETERS:
 * - genre: Filter by book genre (e.g., ?genre=Fiction)
 * - author: Filter by author name (partial match, case-insensitive)
 * - minRating: Minimum rating filter (0-5)
 * - search: Search in title and author fields
 * 
 * @example GET /books?genre=Science&minRating=4.0
 */
function getAllBooks(req, res, next) {
  try {
    let result = [...books]; // Create copy to avoid mutating original array

    // Apply filters if provided
    if (req.query.genre) {
      result = result.filter(book => 
        book.genre.toLowerCase() === req.query.genre.toLowerCase()
      );
    }

    if (req.query.author) {
      const authorSearch = req.query.author.toLowerCase();
      result = result.filter(book => 
        book.author.toLowerCase().includes(authorSearch)
      );
    }

    if (req.query.minRating) {
      const minRating = parseFloat(req.query.minRating);
      if (!isNaN(minRating)) {
        result = result.filter(book => book.rating >= minRating);
      }
    }

    if (req.query.search) {
      const searchTerms = req.query.search.toLowerCase().split(' ');
      result = result.filter(book => 
        searchTerms.every(term => 
          book.title.toLowerCase().includes(term) || 
          book.author.toLowerCase().includes(term)
        )
      );
    }

    // Return paginated results (default: 10 per page)
    const page = parseInt(req.query.page) || 1;
    const limit = parseInt(req.query.limit) || 10;
    const startIndex = (page - 1) * limit;
    const endIndex = startIndex + limit;

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: result.slice(startIndex, endIndex),
      pagination: {
        page,
        limit,
        total: result.length,
        totalPages: Math.ceil(result.length / limit)
      }
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to retrieve books'));
  }
}

/**
 * GET /books/:id - Get a single book by ID.
 * 
 * @param {string} req.params.id - Book ID as string (converted to number)
 */
function getBookById(req, res, next) {
  try {
    const id = parseInt(req.params.id);

    // Validate ID format
    if (isNaN(id)) {
      return next(new NotFoundError('book', req.params.id));
    }

    const book = books.find(b => b.id === id);

    if (!book) {
      return next(new NotFoundError('book', id));
    }

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: book
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to retrieve book'));
  }
}

/**
 * POST /books - Create a new book.
 * 
 * REQUEST BODY:
 * @example
 * {
 *   "title": "The Great Gatsby",
 *   "author": "F. Scott Fitzgerald",
 *   "genre": "Fiction",
 *   "publishedYear": 1925,
 *   "rating": 4.5
 * }
 */
function createBook(req, res, next) {
  try {
    // Check storage limit
    if (books.length >= CONFIG.MAX_BOOKS) {
      return next(new ValidationError('storage', 'Maximum book limit reached'));
    }

    const newBook = {
      id: generateId(),
      title: req.body.title.trim(),
      author: req.body.author.trim(),
      genre: req.body.genre,
      publishedYear: req.body.publishedYear,
      rating: req.body.rating || 0
    };

    books.push(newBook);

    // Return 201 Created with location header for REST compliance
    res.status(201).json({
      success: true,
      data: newBook,
      message: 'Book created successfully'
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to create book'));
  }
}

/**
 * PUT /books/:id - Update an existing book completely.
 * 
 * NOTE: This is a full update, not partial. All required fields must be provided.
 */
function updateBook(req, res, next) {
  try {
    const id = parseInt(req.params.id);

    // Find book by ID
    const bookIndex = books.findIndex(b => b.id === id);

    if (bookIndex === -1) {
      return next(new NotFoundError('book', id));
    }

    // Create updated book object
    const updatedBook = {
      ...books[bookIndex], // Preserve existing fields
      title: req.body.title.trim(),
      author: req.body.author.trim(),
      genre: req.body.genre,
      publishedYear: req.body.publishedYear,
      rating: req.body.rating !== undefined ? req.body.rating : books[bookIndex].rating
    };

    // Update in array
    books[bookIndex] = updatedBook;

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: updatedBook,
      message: 'Book updated successfully'
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to update book'));
  }
}

/**
 * DELETE /books/:id - Delete a book by ID.
 */
function deleteBook(req, res, next) {
  try {
    const id = parseInt(req.params.id);

    // Find book index
    const bookIndex = books.findIndex(b => b.id === id);

    if (bookIndex === -1) {
      return next(new NotFoundError('book', id));
    }

    // Remove book from array
    const deletedBook = books.splice(bookIndex, 1)[0];

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: deletedBook,
      message: 'Book deleted successfully'
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to delete book'));
  }
}

/**
 * GET /stats - Return statistics about the book collection.
 * 
 * Provides aggregate data for monitoring and analytics.
 */
function getStatistics(req, res, next) {
  try {
    if (books.length === 0) {
      return res.json({
        success: true,
        data: {
          totalBooks: 0,
          averageRating: 0,
          genres: {},
          authors: [],
          recentAdditions: []
        }
      });
    }

    // Calculate statistics
    const totalBooks = books.length;
    const averageRating = (books.reduce((sum, book) => sum + book.rating, 0) / totalBooks).toFixed(2);

    // Count by genre
    const genres = {};
    books.forEach(book => {
      genres[book.genre] = (genres[book.genre] || 0) + 1;
    });

    // Get unique authors
    const authors = [...new Set(books.map(book => book.author))];

    // Get recent additions (last 5)
    const recentAdditions = books.slice(-5).reverse();

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: {
        totalBooks,
        averageRating: parseFloat(averageRating),
        genres,
        uniqueAuthors: authors.length,
        authors: authors.slice(0, 10), // Limit to first 10 for response size
        recentAdditions
      }
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(new InternalServerError('Failed to calculate statistics'));
  }
}

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 6: ROUTE DEFINITIONS
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Define all API routes.
 * Routes are organized by resource and HTTP method following REST conventions.
 */

// Health check endpoint (not part of REST resources)
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    success: true,
    data: {
      status: 'healthy',
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      uptime: process.uptime()
    }
  });
});

// Books collection routes
app.get('/books', getAllBooks);                    // List all books
app.post('/books', validateRequest(BOOK_SCHEMA), createBook); // Create book with validation
app.get('/stats', getStatistics);                 // Get statistics

// Single book resource routes (must be defined after collection routes)
app.get('/books/:id', getBookById);               // Get single book
app.put('/books/:id', validateRequest(BOOK_SCHEMA), updateBook); // Update book
app.delete('/books/:id', deleteBook);             // Delete book

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 7: ERROR HANDLING AND SERVER STARTUP
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Catch-all route for undefined endpoints.
 * Returns 404 Not Found with helpful error message.
 */
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  next(new NotFoundError('endpoint', req.originalUrl));
});

/**
 * Global error handling middleware (must be last).
 * Catches all errors and formats consistent responses.
 */
app.use(errorHandler);

// ============================================================================
// SECTION 8: SERVER INITIALIZATION
// ============================================================================

/**
 * Start the HTTP server and listen for connections.
 * Includes startup message with API documentation link.
 */
const server = app.listen(CONFIG.PORT, () => {
  console.log(`📚 Book Management API is running!`);
  console.log(`   🌐 Server: http://localhost:${CONFIG.PORT}`);
  console.log(`   📖 API Docs: http://localhost:${CONFIG.PORT}/docs`);
  console.log(`   🔍 Health Check: http://localhost:${CONFIG.PORT}/health`);
  console.log(`\nAvailable endpoints:`);
  console.log(`   GET    /books          - List all books`);
  console.log(`   POST   /books          - Create new book`);
  console.log(`   GET    /books/:id      - Get single book`);
  console.log(`   PUT    /books/:id      - Update book`);
  console.log(`   DELETE /books/:id      - Delete book`);
  console.log(`   GET    /stats          - Get statistics`);
});

// Graceful shutdown handling
process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  console.log('\n🛑 Shutting down gracefully...');
  server.close(() => {
    console.log('✅ Server closed');
    process.exit(0);
  });
});

process.on('SIGINT', () => {
  console.log('\n🛑 Interrupted, shutting down...');
  server.close(() => {
    process.exit(0);
  });
});

// Export for testing
module.exports = app;
```

## File 3: README.md - Usage Instructions

```markdown
# Book Management REST API

A comprehensive educational example demonstrating REST API design patterns, error handling, validation, and documentation best practices using Node.js and Express.js.

## Features

- ✅ Complete CRUD operations for books
- ✅ In-memory storage with auto-incrementing IDs
- ✅ Comprehensive input validation
- ✅ Custom error classes and middleware
- ✅ Request logging and monitoring
- ✅ CORS support for cross-origin requests
- ✅ Pagination support
- ✅ Filtering and search capabilities
- ✅ Statistics endpoint
- ✅ Detailed JSDoc documentation

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+ 
- npm or yarn package manager

## Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd book-api

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start development server (with auto-restart)
npm run dev

# Or start production server
npm start
```

## API Endpoints

### Health Check
```http
GET /health
```

### Books Collection
```http
GET /books                    # List all books with pagination
POST /books                   # Create new book
GET /stats                    # Get collection statistics
```

### Single Book
```http
GET /books/:id                # Get book by ID
PUT /books/:id                # Update book (full update)
DELETE /books/:id             # Delete book
```

