**REST convention choices explained:**

| Convention | Implementation | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `201 Created` for POST | `res.status(201).json(...)` | Standard HTTP status for resource creation |
| `Location` header | Included in 201 response | Clients can discover the new resource URL |
| Idempotent DELETE | Deleting non-existent returns 404, not error | Safe to retry; matches HTTP spec |
| Partial PUT body | Merge with existing data | Practical UX; strict PUT would require all fields |
| Structured JSON responses | `{ success, data, meta }` shape | Consistent contract for API consumers |

